; Iter 31 slow-zone hazard. Passive Area2D that halves hero walk speed
; while inside. Visual = murky green/teal pool with a slow ripple ring
; + two bubble pips that pulse out of sync.
;
; Iter-readability pass: zone is ALWAYS active (no telegraph state) so
; the goal is "persistently visible bounded ground threat with subtle
; motion that says SLOWING MAGIC." Added Swirl marks rotating slowly
; around the rim — instantly disambiguates "this is a magical drag
; field" from any dark decor patch.
;
; Children (back-to-front):
;   CollisionShape2D — circular detection at radius 36.
;   FootprintHalo (Polygon2D, z=1) — extra-wide soft outer halo so the
;     zone's bounds read at a glance even on a busy floor.
;   Pool (Polygon2D) — main murky disc, mid-dark teal at 70% alpha.
;   PoolRim (Line2D) — soft darker outline so the pool reads against
;     the floor.
;   Swirl (Node2D wrapper) — rotates a few wisp polygons around the
;     center to communicate "magic field, slowing you."
;   RippleRing (Polygon2D) — inner ring polygon; script modulates its
;     alpha and scale for a slow breathing pulse.
;   BubbleA / BubbleB — small bright dots offset from center, script
;     modulates their alpha sin-waves at different phases so they
;     read as gas pockets surfacing.

; Iter 59 — z_index back to default 0. The iter-58 fix (setting z=-1)
; accidentally pushed the pool BELOW the static procedural_dungeon
; Background sprite at z=0, making the slow_zone completely invisible
; on the floor. Hero-on-top is now solved via tree-order: main.gd
; moves the hero to the END of the children list after spawns, so
; the hero (later in tree) draws above hazards (earlier in tree)
; at the same z=0.
[node name="SlowZone" type="Area2D"]
collision_layer = 0
collision_mask = 2
monitorable = false
script = ExtResource("1_script")

[node name="CollisionShape2D" type="CollisionShape2D" parent="."]
shape = SubResource("slowzone_area")

; ── Iter 186 batch 2 — carved-stone basin frame ───────────────────────
; Pre-iter-186 the slow zone was a 5-layer Polygon2D pool that read as
; "procedural shape painted on the floor" — directive critique 4: "the
; central hazard lacks identity, doesn't feel embedded in the world."
; New: a stone rim ring + 4 cardinal rune marks suggest the hazard is
; a CARVED RITUAL BASIN, not a paint stain. The toxic pool sits INSIDE
; a real architectural feature.

; StoneRim — thick dark Line2D ring at radius 42 (just outside the
; Pool's 38). 6 px width reads as a chunky chiseled lip around the
; basin. Closed = true joins ends seamlessly. Drawn at z = 0 so it
; sits ABOVE the FootprintHalo (z=1) — wait, FootprintHalo z=1 means
; halo above StoneRim. Tree order: StoneRim added BEFORE FootprintHalo
; below, so even at same z=0 the rim draws first / below. The halo
; alpha 0.22 lets the stone rim show through faintly even through it.
[node name="StoneRim" type="Line2D" parent="."]
